title: "pricing-experiments-synthetic-panel: Synthetic Panel Data Generator for Pricing Experiments"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-19
url: "https://github.com/pedrocadahia/pricing-experiments-synthetic-panel"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pedrocadahia/pricing-experiments-synthetic-panel"
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
keywords:
  - synthetic-data
  - price-elasticity
  - causal-inference
  - double-machine-learning
  - pass-through
  - panel-data
  - revenue-growth-management
abstract: >-
  Reproducible data-generating processes for price-elasticity research on weekly
  retail panels. Three generators produce a common SKU x region x week schema with
  a known ground truth and deliberately embedded identification regimes (clean,
  weak, sticky shelf, confounded, collinear), so that estimators can be scored not
  only on bias and coverage but on whether they correctly abstain where the data
  cannot identify anything.
